{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"grayish-candid-pittabird","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## What\n\nWiden `_OPERATOR_ATTESTED_TAG_RE` (`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/det_operator_attested.py:45`) to\n`\\[(?:non-codebase|operator-attested)\\]`, and widen the `.rebar/criteria_routing.json:75`\nactivation trigger `text_all` to match either spelling.\n\n## Why this is the keystone\n\nAll four deterministic consumers share the IDENTICAL compiled regex object — `decide_ops`,\n`workflow_ops`, `det_attestation_launder`, `det_measurement_provenance` each satisfy `is`\nagainst it. One pattern change propagates to every consumer with no new branch anywhere, which\nis why `det_floor.py` (793/800 LOC cap) and `decide_ops.plan_review_decide` (complexity 21,\ngrandfathered) need no edits and their gates do not fire.\n\n## Trap\n\nThe alternation MUST be non-capturing. `decide_ops.operator_attested_ac_texts` uses `findall()`,\nwhich returns TUPLES if the group captures, silently breaking Pass-3 enrichment.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `_OPERATOR_ATTESTED_TAG_RE` matches `- [ ] [non-codebase] x` and `- [ ] [operator-attested] x`\n      case-insensitively, and does NOT match the `[operator_attested]` underscore near-miss.\n- [ ] `operator_attested_ac_texts` returns a `list[str]` (not tuples) for a description mixing\n      both spellings, proved by a test asserting element types.\n- [ ] The `.rebar/criteria_routing.json` `project.measurement-provenance` trigger fires on a\n      plan tagged `[non-codebase]` and on one tagged `[operator-attested]`, proved by a test.\n- [ ] All existing tests pass unchanged.","id":"3726-a1b0-c9bb-4d83","parent_id":"6f5a-4a49-7bbf-4a30","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"S1 — widen the canonical tag matcher to accept [non-codebase] and [operator-attested]"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787185925190577001,"uuid":"a0f39118-887a-4795-b9ef-e21d200588e1"}